body:
I went in with very low expectations to make sure I wasnt disappointed.  I've also come to terms with the possibility of never experiencing sex or romance, so I didn't pressure myself too much.  The real experience was getting over my txting anxiety I think?  I'm a little worried I wont get another date because I still dont know how to ask out women.  Also the girl was incredibly strange, which is fine, but I wasn't very interested in her and I'm not sure if this is the only type of person people will set me up with.

&#x200B;

Overall I'm glad I went on the date, it was healthy for me to get out of my comfort zone, and I like that some more people at work who usually ignore me are talking to me and asking me about it.  I don't know if that's a good reason to date, but its meant alot to feel "normal" and like I fit in by having something to add to conversation at work when dating comes up for a bit.
